  "description": "<p>\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Description:</span> Simple breakout board for the MQ - 3, MQ - 4, MQ - 6 and MQ - 7 gas sensors.&nbsp; All you need is VCC at 5V, GND, and a resistor to an ADC, that is it.<br />\n\n\n\t<br />\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Note: </span>This is the PCB only. Sensors listed below.<br style=\"font-weight: bold;\" />\n\n\n\t<br />\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Dimensions:</span> 16.8mm diameter<br />\n\n\n\t<br />\n\n\n\t<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Documents:</span></p>\n\n\n<ul>\n\n\n\t<li>\n\n\n\t\t<a classname=\"\" href=\"http://www.sparkfun.com/datasheets/BreakoutBoards/Gas_Sensor_Breakout-v11.pdf\" name=\"\" target=\"_blank\">Schematic</a></li>\n\n\n\t<li>\n\n\n\t\t<a href=\"http://wiring.org.co/learning/basics/airqualitymq135.html\" target=\"_blank\">Wiring Example</a></li>\n\n\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>\n\n\n\t<br />\n\n\n\t&nbsp;</p>",
